      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes a transactional mechanism used by the guarded tool executor to ensure all-or-nothing semantics for file writes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core Function**: Before any file is overwritten, the system records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback Capability**: If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting any newly created files.\n\n**Implementation**: This provides transaction-like guarantees without needing a database, using the in-memory journal as a transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Note**: The page also mentions that the Query agent itself never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library available to agents that do write.",
